      "description": "Most agencies don't need client onboarding software until they run about 10 concurrent onboardings. Rocketlane, GUIDEcx, Dock and Arrows compared.",
      "abstract": "Client onboarding software is a category of tool that moves a new client from signed contract to live engagement: shared task lists, document collection, a client-facing portal, and a timeline everyone can see. Most agencies and professional services firms don't need one. The honest trigger is volume and headcount, not ambition: once you're running more than roughly 10 concurrent onboardings with more than one internal team touching each one, a spreadsheet and an inbox stop being able to hold it, and a dedicated tool earns its cost. Below that line, a good template inside the project management tool you already pay for usually beats buying something new.",
